// The Books: Hand to Hand — the lineage of the books that carried the wing's
// alphabets.
//
// From the wing's research file the-books.verified.json. Not an alphabet: the
// units are the books (and the few manuscripts) of the lineage, one card each,
// in date order. Each card's `value` says what the book carried, `translit`
// gives its place and date in short, `numeric` is its year, and formConfidence
// grades the card's facts; nothing is drawn, so every card has glyph: null.
// The same books, with their descriptions, datings, the alphabets they carry
// (registry keys) and their digitised copies, are the `transmission` timeline.
//
// Left out because what they print could not be checked against a copy:
// Postel 1538, Vigenère 1586, Rocca 1591, de Bry 1596, the 1550 Latin
// Agrippa, Bartolocci 1675, Sefer Raziel 1701, the Shawq al-mustahām and
// Hammer 1806; also Tory 1529 (kept only as a disputed claim), Westcott's
// copies in Ars Quatuor Coronatorum (1890, reported only by Blavatsky) and
// Tyson 1993 (named only for its translator). The northern and insular strands (the Galdrabók, Worm, List,
// O'Flaherty, Graves) and Crowley are followed on their own pages, not here.
// The three Internet Archive scans the fact-check withheld (b30335231,
// b24884339, the 1801 Barrett) are not linked.
